<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-09-29T03:43:04+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 29 Sep 2026 03:43:04 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[In 1930, former Maine governor Percival Baxter bought nearly 6,000 acres around Mount Katahdin]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134549933.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Percival P. Baxter dedicated over thirty years of his life to creating Baxter State Park in Maine, now one of North America's largest state parks. His vision was to maintain the land's natural beauty, thwarting industrial encroachment and promoting sustainable forestry. Though he passed away in 1969, his legacy endures as the park continues to thrive, expanding through land trades and acquisitions to cover over 209,000 acres of pristine wilderness.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1930-former-maine-governor-percival-baxter-bought-nearly-6000-acres-around-mount-katahdin-32-years-later-his-final-acquisition-brought-his-gifted-parkland-to-201018-acres-now-part-of-a-209644-acre-park/articleshow/134549933.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1930-former-maine-governor-percival-baxter-bought-nearly-6000-acres-around-mount-katahdin-32-years-later-his-final-acquisition-brought-his-gifted-parkland-to-201018-acres-now-part-of-a-209644-acre-park/articleshow/134549933.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-29T01:21:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134549971,imgsize-2102719.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A 1914 Massachusetts mansion built after a high-society scandal is listed for $3.5 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134548927.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A stunning Gilded Age estate known as The Crossways has hit the market for a price tag of $3.5 million. This historic home, built in 1914, is deeply connected to Hopedale's Draper family. It showcases exquisite original craftsmanship, alongside modern amenities like central air and hydro-air heating. Nestled on 2.36 acres, it boasts beautifully designed Italian gardens and an inviting outdoor pool, reflecting Hopedale's rich industrial history.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/a-1914-massachusetts-mansion-built-after-a-high-society-scandal-is-listed-for-3-5-million-the-10269-square-foot-estate-has-12-bedrooms-italian-gardens-and-a-39-foot-ballroom/articleshow/134548927.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/a-1914-massachusetts-mansion-built-after-a-high-society-scandal-is-listed-for-3-5-million-the-10269-square-foot-estate-has-12-bedrooms-italian-gardens-and-a-39-foot-ballroom/articleshow/134548927.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-29T01:06:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134549930,imgsize-1482906.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ohio lawyer sent $550 to a stranger on Zelle; it sparked a 3-year court battle]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134544859.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-ohio-lawyer-accidentally-sent-550-to-a-stranger-on-zelle-the-payment-mistake-turned-into-a-three-year-court-battle/articleshow/134544859.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-ohio-lawyer-accidentally-sent-550-to-a-stranger-on-zelle-the-payment-mistake-turned-into-a-three-year-court-battle/articleshow/134544859.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-28T22:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134545201,imgsize-1200447.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A Texas oil geologist first saw McKittrick Canyon in 1921, later bought the land for a private retreat]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134547499.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 1921, petroleum geologist Wallace Pratt was captivated by the stunning landscape of McKittrick Canyon. He subsequently partnered to acquire land which led to the establishment of family homes. Commencing in 1959, Pratt generously began donating his land for conservation, culminating in the 1972 creation of Guadalupe Mountains National Park. Today, his former residences stand preserved within the park, serving as valuable educational resources.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-texas-oil-geologist-first-saw-mckittrick-canyon-in-1921-later-bought-the-land-for-a-private-retreat-38-years-later-he-donated-4942-acres-and-his-home-helping-create-guadalupe-mountains-national-park/articleshow/134547499.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-texas-oil-geologist-first-saw-mckittrick-canyon-in-1921-later-bought-the-land-for-a-private-retreat-38-years-later-he-donated-4942-acres-and-his-home-helping-create-guadalupe-mountains-national-park/articleshow/134547499.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-28T23:48:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134548896,imgsize-845228.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[FBI co-deputy director Andrew Bailey resigns after just over a year, says ‘returning to family in Missouri’]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134548235.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/fbi-co-deputy-director-andrew-bailey-resigns-after-just-over-a-year-says-returning-to-family-in-missouri/articleshow/134548235.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/fbi-co-deputy-director-andrew-bailey-resigns-after-just-over-a-year-says-returning-to-family-in-missouri/articleshow/134548235.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-28T23:04:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134548318,imgsize-829753.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NYT tech executive shot dead allegedly by Chinese in-laws at California sports complex; shooters took turns to spray bullets]]></title><description>&lt;img border=